\ Exercise the strict-AOT compound-fallback build error: in
\ --interpreter-fallback=false mode, a compiled caller that dispatches
\ to an uncompiled compound callee must fail the build with a diagnostic
\ that names the caller, the callee, the line, and the callee's
\ NotCompilableReason. `print-line` reaches `stream-write-string`, whose
\ compiled body falls back to `>bytes` and `stream-write`; `flush` calls
\ `stream-flush`. Today those callees are uncompilable, so this test
\ asserts they surface as build errors instead of runtime fallback.
"ok" print-line
